  "description": "A liquid-mercury mirror reflecting the image. The surface is a true capillary wave (height + velocity wave equation): click launches, the held pointer's press and treble-driven rain drops ring outward on their own, while analytic capillary packets travel across it. Fresnel horizon reflection: steep glancing slopes stop mirroring the image and pick up a cool-top / warm-floor studio gradient. Specular glints ride the crests; generated depth follows the wave energy (stylized, not a physical fluid model).",
